<%# Testing gates — the task-owned gate VERDICTS (GateRun: G1 Cert, DoR builder,
    DoR review, G2a Primary, G2b Light), the sibling of the testing-phases card
    above: phases are duration telemetry, gates are attempt-aware pass/fail records
    with the test SOPs each attempt executed. Rendered only once at least one gate
    has a run. %>
<% gate_runs = (task_gate_runs || {}) %>
<% if gate_runs.any? %>
  <div class="card p-6 mb-6">
    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Testing gates</h3>
      <span class="text-[10px] text-muted uppercase tracking-wide">gate verdicts</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted text-xs mb-4">
      The task-owned gates and their latest attempt — G1 Cert (full suite + lint) → DoR (builder + review gate-zero) → G2 Review (primary + light).
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <% GateRun::TASK_KEYS.each do |key| %>
        <% run = gate_runs[key] %>
        <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-lg p-3">
          <p class="label-upper"><%= GateRun::GATES.dig(key, "label") %></p>
          <p class="text-heading text-sm font-semibold"><%= gate_attempt_label(run) || "—" %></p>
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide <%= gate_status_class(run) %>">
            <%= run ? run.status.humanize : "Not run" %>
          </p>
          <% if run && run.sops.any? %>
            <details class="mt-2">
              <summary class="text-[10px] text-muted uppercase tracking-wide cursor-pointer select-none">
                <%= pluralize(run.sops.size, "SOP") %>
              </summary>
              <ul class="mt-1 space-y-0.5">
                <% run.sops.each do |entry| %>
                  <%# THE GLYPH CHAIN IS AN ALLOW-LIST, AND SINCE
                      /tasks/pending-ci-paints-check IT DEFAULTS TO `?`, NOT `✓`.

                      `pass` and `fail` are the only VERDICTS. Everything else is one of two
                      families, and neither is an outcome:

                        IN FLIGHT (GateRun::IN_FLIGHT_RESULTS → ◌) — the answer is COMING.
                          `running`, a cert lane that started (or was ABANDONED); `pending`,
                          CI checks GitHub has not settled. The remedy is to WAIT.
                        NO VERDICT (GateRun::NO_VERDICT_RESULTS → ⚠) — the answer was never
                          GIVEN. CI was never READ (`unreadable` — the credential was
                          refused), never SPOKE (`no_checks` — the PR reported none yet;
                          `unverified` — `gh` fell over), or never had a PR to run against at
                          all (`no_pr` — devops.pr_url is blank). The remedy is to go find
                          out WHY. None may be a ✓ (a CI nobody heard is not a CI that
                          passed) and none may be an ✗ (the false red
                          /tasks/gate-logs-auth-as-red, /tasks/refused-review-records-fail and
                          /tasks/no-pr-records-as-fail took out of the record).

                      WHY THE DEFAULT FLIPPED, which was the whole of
                      /tasks/pending-ci-paints-check. This chain used to end
                      `else ["✓", …]`, so `pass` and every UNCLASSIFIED value shared one arm.
                      Four consecutive defects arrived that way: a value was added upstream,
                      nobody added an arm here, and the row rendered as a PASS. `pending` was
                      the fourth — a CI still RUNNING, painted in the permanent record as one
                      that passed, which is the direction nobody audits.

                      Adding the missing arm fixes the instance; moving the default fixes the
                      CLASS. `pass` is now an EXPLICIT arm and the fall-through is `?`, so a
                      value this file has never heard of renders as what it actually is — an
                      unknown — instead of as the strongest positive claim the card can make.
                      An empty/absent `result` lands here too, by design: `nil.to_s` is "",
                      and `bin/gate show` has always printed that as `-` rather than a pass.

                      NOTE THE ASYMMETRY WITH THE PRODUCER, deliberately. CiGate.gate_row's
                      own `else` still answers "fail"/"unverified" for an unclassified STATE,
                      and that stays: it is a GATE, an allow-list defaults to REFUSE, and a
                      loud refusal is what gets an arm added. This is a RENDERER — it refuses
                      nothing, it only tells an auditor what happened — so its conservative
                      direction is not "fail", it is "I do not know". Same word, opposite risk:
                      a gate that cannot classify must refuse; a record that cannot classify
                      must say so rather than congratulate. %>
                  <% result = entry["result"].to_s %>
                  <% glyph, tone = if result == "fail" then ["✗", "text-rose-400"]
                                   elsif result == "pass" then ["✓", "text-emerald-400"]
                                   elsif GateRun::IN_FLIGHT_RESULTS.include?(result) then ["◌", "text-amber-400"]
                                   elsif GateRun::NO_VERDICT_RESULTS.include?(result) then ["⚠", "text-amber-400"]
                                   else ["?", "text-muted"]
                                   end %>
                  <li class="text-[11px] text-muted flex items-baseline gap-1" data-result="<%= result %>">
                    <span class="<%= tone %>" data-test="gate-sop-glyph"><%= glyph %></span>
                    <span class="text-body"><%= entry["sop"] %></span>
                    <% if (sop_duration = gate_sop_duration_label(entry["duration_ms"])) %>
                      <span><%= sop_duration %></span>
                    <% end %>
                  </li>
                <% end %>
              </ul>
            </details>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
